{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "GAL",
  "chapter": 6,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "GAL.6.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.6.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Brethren, if a man be overtaken in a fault, ye who are spiritual, restore such one in the spirit of meekness; considering thyself, lest thou also be tempted.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.6.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.6.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Bear ye one another's burdens, and so fulfill the law of Christ.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.6.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.6.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For if a man thinketh himself to be something, when he is nothing, he deceiveth himself.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.6.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.6.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But let every man prove his own work, and then shall he have rejoicing in himself alone, and not in another.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.6.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.6.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For every man shall bear his own burden.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.6.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.6.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let him that is taught in the word communicate to him that teacheth in all good things.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.6.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.6.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be not deceived; God is not mocked: for whatever a man soweth, that shall he also reap.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.6.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.6.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he that soweth to his flesh shall from the flesh reap corruption: but he that soweth to the Spirit, shall from the Spirit reap life everlasting.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.6.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.6.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And let us not be weary in well-doing: for in due season we shall reap, if we faint not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.6.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.6.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As we have therefore opportunity, let us do good to all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", especially to them who are of the household of faith.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.6.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.6.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye see how large a letter I have written to you with my own hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.6.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.6.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As many as desire to make a fair show in the flesh, they constrain you to be circumcised; only lest they should suffer persecution for the cross of Christ.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.6.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.6.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For neither they themselves who are circumcised keep the law; but desire to have you circumcised, that they may glory in your flesh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.6.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.6.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But may it never be that I should glory, save in the cross of our Lord Jesus Christ, by whom the world is crucified to me, and I to the world.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.6.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.6.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For in Christ Jesus neither circumcision availeth any thing, nor uncircumcision, but a new creature.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.6.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.6.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And as many as walk according to this rule, peace ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on them, and mercy, and upon the Israel of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.6.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.6.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "From henceforth let no man trouble me: for I bear in my body the marks of the Lord Jesus.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.6.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.6.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Brethren, the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with your spirit. Amen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
